== 8.9 Chapter 8 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Which of the following is not a cell?],
  [Yeast],
  [Bacterium],
  [Virus],
  [Amoeba]
)

#mcq(2, [Bacteria differ from viruses in that bacteria],
  [are always harmful],
  [have a nucleus],
  [are cells and can reproduce outside a host],
  [contain chlorophyll]
)

#mcq(3, [The single loop of DNA in a bacterium lies],
  [inside the cell wall],
  [inside a nucleus],
  [free in the cytoplasm],
  [inside the flagellum]
)

#mcq(4, [A fungus is made up of threads called],
  [hyphae],
  [flagella],
  [hyaline],
  [cilia]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of these is a single-celled fungus?],
  [Mould],
  [Yeast],
  [Mushroom],
  [Penicillium]
)

#mcq(6, [Decay is best described as],
  [the drying of dead matter],
  [the breakdown of dead organic matter by micro-organisms],
  [the burning of dead matter],
  [the freezing of dead matter]
)

#mcq(7, [Decay is a form of],
  [transpiration],
  [respiration],
  [photosynthesis],
  [digestion in animals]
)

#mcq(8, [The gas released during decay is mainly],
  [nitrogen],
  [hydrogen],
  [oxygen],
  [carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(9, [A compost heap becomes warm because],
  [water is evaporating],
  [the sun heats the heap],
  [respiration by decomposers releases heat],
  [the plants are still photosynthesising]
)

#mcq(10, [The mineral salts released by decay are important because they],
  [kill soil bacteria],
  [are used by plants to make proteins and other compounds],
  [give the soil its colour],
  [make the soil lighter]
)

#mcq(11, [Which condition is removed by salting food?],
  [Moisture],
  [Oxygen],
  [Warmth],
  [Food]
)

#mcq(12, [Food is preserved by canning because canning],
  [freezes the food],
  [adds vitamins],
  [removes oxygen and the heat kills the micro-organisms],
  [makes the food acidic]
)

#mcq(13, [Which of these is a method of preservation by removing warmth?],
  [Refrigeration],
  [Salting],
  [Smoking],
  [Adding vinegar]
)

#mcq(14, [Smoking preserves fish because the smoke],
  [freezes the fish],
  [dries the fish and contains antibacterial chemicals],
  [adds protein],
  [makes the fish sweeter]
)

#mcq(15, [The gas that makes bread dough rise is],
  [oxygen],
  [methane],
  [nitrogen],
  [carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(16, [The micro-organism used in making yoghurt is],
  [lactic-acid bacteria],
  [yeast],
  [a virus],
  [a mould]
)

#mcq(17, [Biogas is produced from animal and plant waste by],
  [yeast],
  [anaerobic bacteria],
  [fungi],
  [aerobic bacteria]
)

#mcq(18, [Penicillin was originally obtained from],
  [a protozoan],
  [a bacterium],
  [a virus],
  [a mould]
)

#mcq(19, [Nitrogen-fixing bacteria in the root nodules of legumes],
  [produce methane],
  [cause the plant to rot],
  [convert nitrogen gas to nitrates the plant can use],
  [release nitrogen into the air]
)

#mcq(20, [Which of these would slow the growth of micro-organisms least?],
  [Keeping the food warm and moist],
  [Adding strong sugar solution],
  [Drying the food],
  [Freezing the food]
)

#mcq(21, [Milk turns sour on a hot day because],
  [the water evaporates],
  [the fat turns to sugar],
  [the milk absorbs oxygen faster],
  [bacteria multiply faster and produce acid]
)

#mcq(22, [Food poisoning caused by badly canned food is often due to],
  [yeast],
  [a protozoan],
  [a virus],
  [Clostridium botulinum]
)

#mcq(23, [The phase of a growth curve in which the number of bacteria doubles at a constant rate is the],
  [lag phase],
  [log phase],
  [death phase],
  [stationary phase]
)

#mcq(24, [In the stationary phase of a bacterial culture],
  [the cells are adjusting to the medium],
  [the cells are dividing fastest],
  [all the cells are dead],
  [births equal deaths]
)

#mcq(25, [Micro-organisms are best described as],
  [organisms that live in water],
  [organisms too small to be seen with the naked eye],
  [organisms that cause disease],
  [organisms with no nucleus]
)

#mcq(26, [Which of the following is not a product of the decay of a dead leaf?],
  [Chlorophyll],
  [Water],
  [Carbon dioxide],
  [Mineral salts]
)

#mcq(27, [A student keeps two pieces of bread, one in a sealed dry tin and one in a moist warm tin. Mould grows only on the second. This shows that],
  [mould needs light],
  [mould grows only on bread],
  [mould needs moisture and warmth],
  [mould needs salt]
)

#mcq(28, [Which of these is a useful role of bacteria in agriculture?],
  [Causing foot-and-mouth disease],
  [Spoiling silage],
  [Breaking down organic matter in compost],
  [Causing rust in wheat]
)

#mcq(29, [Pasteurisation of milk involves],
  [freezing the milk],
  [adding salt to the milk],
  [boiling the milk for an hour],
  [heating the milk to about 72 °C for a short time and cooling it quickly]
)

#mcq(30, [The main reason micro-organisms are important in the carbon cycle is that they],
  [store carbon in rocks],
  [prevent photosynthesis],
  [return carbon to the atmosphere as carbon dioxide],
  [fix carbon from the air]
)

